<title>UK: Comerica sets $100 million five-year FRN. [CORRECTED 9:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>Comerica sets $100 million five-year FRN. [CORRECTED 9:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers Lehman Brothers and Sanwa International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   COMERICA</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY   *03.MAR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     0.03125   PAY DATE    03.MAR.97</p>
<p>(Corrects margin from 0.3125)</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.9825   FULL FEES   17.5 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALLABLE FROM MARCH 2000 AT PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES	DIRECT, UNCONDITIONAL AND UNSECURED</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
